%% -*- mode: erlang -*-
%%
%% MACAO. What this port declares about itself.
%%
%% Read with file:consult/1 and handed straight to tom_market:open/1. One term,
%% and every field in it is physical.
%%
%% NOTHING HERE IS A PRICE, and tom_market drops anything that is not one of the
%% six words below on the way in. town is a headcount as a multiple of a
%% standard town; hinterland is an extent of land; a yield is what a standard
%% hinterland turns out per tick. Not one of them says what anything is worth,
%% and the exponent between a yield and a price is 0.556, so no yield here could
%% be nudged toward a price even on purpose.
%%
%% THE CENSUS IS SURVEYED AND IT MATTERS THAT IT IS COMPLETE. A good listed here
%% has been looked for; a good left out has not, and an unsurveyed good is
%% priced at the scarce end, because the only supply this port knows of is what
%% turns up with no source at all. cannon are {0, 0} on purpose: this port
%% looked and no harbour anywhere makes them, so they have no geography and the
%% declared yield is already the artisan rate everywhere.
%%
%% The eight goods are the slice the mechanism's own worked example uses, and
%% these numbers reproduce it: musk goes for 12.9155 here and 172.90 at Lisbon,
%% out of a yield and a census and nothing else.

#{town => 2.0,
  hinterland => 1.2,

  goods => #{rice => 400.0,
             musk => 0.5,
             nutmeg => 40.0,
             copper => 30.0,
             quicksilver => 1.2,
             silver_ore => 900.0,
             cannon => 0.02,
             tin => 20.0},

  %% The Pearl River mouth. Everything Chinese leaves through here.
  produces => [musk, quicksilver],

  %% How many OTHER harbours make each good, split into this port's own region
  %% and everywhere beyond it. Coastal traffic against a voyage.
  census => #{rice => {0, 3},
              musk => {1, 0},
              nutmeg => {0, 4},
              copper => {0, 2},
              quicksilver => {1, 0},
              silver_ore => {0, 2},
              cannon => {0, 0},
              tin => {0, 2}},

  factories => []}.
